# Upstream references (EIP convenience vs AA vs privacy)

## MetaMask-family convenience layer — allowed

For wallet UX / provider convenience (EIP-1559 fee heuristics, speed presets,
EIP-1193 method shapes, common dApp interop quirks), battle-tested **MetaMask /
ethers / Alloy** algorithms and patterns are approved references.

- Reimplement in Rust on allowlisted crates (`alloy`, etc.).
- Cite the algorithm family in a short comment or module doc.
- Do not copy proprietary MetaMask extension UI code.
- Do not treat Ambire or Kohaku as the source for fee/provider convenience.

Authoritative copy lives in `CLAUDE.md` engineering rule 6.

## Ambire vs Kohaku — product pair ≠ code couple

Originally a complementary product pair (Ambire AA + Kohaku privacy). They remain
orthogonal layers:

| Piece | Role |
|---|---|
| **Ambire** (`vaughan-aa`) | EIP-7702 smart accounts + atomic batched sends. ABI/interop only. |
| **Kohaku** | Deferred as a crate. Stealth is in-core ERC-5564; RAILGUN NO-GO. |

Ambire does not unblock Kohaku/RAILGUN. See `docs/kohaku-go-no-go.md` and
`docs/ambire-aa.md`.